{
  "title": "Spawn zones",
  "url": "https://valheim.fandom.com/wiki/Spawn_zones",
  "slug": "Spawn_zones",
  "categories": [
    "Mechanics"
  ],
  "infobox": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Each zone has its own spawners that depend on its biome. Spawners are active depending on the time of day, weather and world progression. Spawns are prevented with player bases."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Zones",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "The map is split up into 64x64 grid squares with 0,0 being in the center of the first zone.\nEvery 4 seconds, zones with a player process their spawners."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spawners",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Each spawner tries spawning if enough time has passed since its previous spawning attempt.\nAmount of tries is calculated from the elapsed time and capped at creature limit.\nFor example, Deer have a spawn interval of 100 seconds. After 250 seconds, 2 spawn attempts would be made. After 500 seconds, only 4 spawn attempts would be made because the limit is 4."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spawn attempts",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "A spawn attempt fails if:\n• The random roll fails\n• Required boss has not been killed\n• Wrong weather\n• Wrong time of the day\n• Too many same creatures already exist in loaded zones (creature limit)\n• Valid spawn position is not found after 20 attempts\n• There is already the same creature too close to the valid spawn position (suppression limit)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Valid spawn position",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "A spawn position is randomly selected between 40 - 80 meters of a random player in the zone. Spawn position is not valid if:\n• Position has a wrong biome\n• The zone of the position has multiple biomes (if a full biome is required)\n• Covered by a structure\n• Blocked by player base\n• Wrong altitude\n• Wrong terrain angle (max tilt 35 degrees by default)\n• Wrong amount of water\n• A player exists within 40 meters\n• Position is not inside a forest (if a forest is required). Forests are determined on world generation, terraforming or the amount of planted trees have no effect.\nNote: Terraforming with a Cultivator, Hoe or Pickaxes does not directly block spawning but affects terrain altitude and angle."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Group size",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "The amount of creatures is randomly selected from the group size. The amount is capped at creature limit.\nWith only one creature, the enemy is spawned at the valid spawn position.\nWith more than one creature, the game tries finding a spawn position two times for each creature. The spawn position is randomly selected from a circle around the initial spawn position (group radius). Same rules apply for determining the validity."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Spawning",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Each spawned creature has 10% chance to level up (9% for 1 star, 1% for 2 stars), if leveling up is allowed. For some creatures, the leveling up requires enough distance from the world center.\nIf the spawner is only active during the night, then spawned creatures are set to despawn during the daytime (as long as their zone is active).\nFlying enemies are spawned off the ground depending on the creature. The actual spawn position is still on the ground and can be blocked by a player base."
    },
