      "heading": "Example",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "For example Serpents have two spawners which only work when zone is located in Ocean biome. The first spawner works only during the night while the second spawner only works during storms. This means both spawners are active during night time storms giving the best chance for finding a Serpent.\nSerpent spawners work every 1000 seconds and only have a 5% chance to work. If you just wait on a spot then it can take hours for a Serpent to spawn. But if you keep moving to new zones then you can easily get a spawn attempt every 12-16 seconds (depending on the speed). However this requires that you have not visited the area for 1000 seconds.\nSerpents can spawn up to 80 meters away so it is good to be in a middle of the ocean. If you are near other biomes then the spawn can fail because of wrong biome. Serpents never spawn as starred variant because the max level is 1.\nSerpents that spawn because of storm will not despawn on morning even when spawned during the night (but no way to tell which spawner spawned it).\nA serpent suppresses other serpent spawns within 50 meters. It is still possible to spawn more serpents (since they can spawn up to 80 meters away) but the chances are drastically reduced. Serpents detect you up to 50 meters away so most of the time they will not aggro right away."
    }
